  "notes": "Tier 3 is the default -- only Tier 1, 2, and 4 are listed. This file is a FLOOR over the derived tier (salary for NFL/NBA, club for PREMIER_LEAGUE, card position for UFC), never a ceiling: it is consulted BEFORE those, so an entry set below what an athlete rates actively suppresses them. Tier 4 is not merely 'depth player' -- it sits above thresholds.default.max_tier and DROPS BREAKING outright, so deleting a Tier 4 entry expands coverage rather than tidying it. Entries are deliberately KEPT for athletes who have left a roster: a Tier 1/2 entry is what keeps TRACKING alive for their injury history (Tier 3 is tier_blocked for TRACKING), and a Tier 4 entry keeps the block. PREMIER_LEAGUE lists Tier 1 only for the globally marquee, plus Tier 2 for stars OUTSIDE the six clubs that derive Tier 2 from significance-config.json derived_tiers -- big-six squad players need no entry. Spellings must match ESPN's (accents included); normalization strips diacritics on both sides, but 'Odegaard' and 'Ødegaard' do NOT normalize alike. Audit with: npx tsx src/scripts/tier-file-audit.ts. Approved by founder 2026-04-29; salary-alignment pass 2026-08-13; Premier League pass 2026-08-15.",
